      "side": 1,
      "message": "For the vendor patchlevel, having the HAL service send over the value from getVendorPatchlevel() should be OK -- that\u0027s what I\u0027m doing in the corresponding change to the Cuttlefish HAL service (aosp/1730092).  (However, watch out that the property that the value is retrieved from may need an SELinux policy change to access.)\n\nOn a real/physical device, the bootloader should send the boot patchlevel across to the keymint TA at start of day.  I don\u0027t know what the software-only equivalent should be -- for Cuttlefish I\u0027m currently just setting 0 (but I\u0027ve asked the question as to whether there could be a better option).",
